(PRC-63 — the two decoder functions the manual gives compile and return
 the exit code and the terminating signal.
 Also covers: PRC-62 (the compiler knows nothing about the wait-status
 encoding; this decodes the raw word with divide, modulo and bit-and, with
 nothing installed — no `see`, no library).
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-63.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   exit code 9
   signal 0
)
To 'exit code of' with a number called status.
  Return a number, status divide 256 modulo 256.

To 'signal of' with a number called status.
  Return a number, status bit-and 127.

a number called 'the child' is fork the process.
If 'the child' is 0 then, Exit 9.
a number called reaped is reap child 'the child'.
a number called status is the reaped status.
print "exit code {'exit code of' of status}".
print "signal {'signal of' of status}".
